// §5.39: the same function declared twice in one scope.
//
// The `fn` half of the duplicate-declaration finding. This used to print 2.
// Serez has no overloading, so two `fn`s of one name are a collision rather
// than a signature set, and nothing here inspects parameters.
fn int duplicated() { return 1; }
fn int duplicated() { return 2; }
out duplicated();
